# Federation key material. scripts/generate_identities.py writes secrets/ into the repository
# root, and the documented workflow is exactly that followed by `docker compose up --build`.
# Without these lines every private Ed25519 key, plus the plaintext transport keys in
# compose.env, is packed into the build context and kept in the BuildKit context cache.
# Nothing COPYs them into an image, but a build context is not a private place.
# .gitignore excludes the same paths.
secrets
**/*_identity.json
roster.json
compose.env
*.md
!README.md
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.semgrep
Makefile
tasks.py
